# GENERIC UNIT — safe to sync verbatim on deploy: no deployment-specific value lives here. The door, the
# listener and every hostname come from EnvironmentFile=%h/.env, which is where a SERVER's configuration
# lives (INSTALL.md §3; render-units.mjs defaults --env to the same file).
#
# ── WHY THIS UNIT EXISTS (tracker issue 1925) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# It did not, and that was the gap under the whole issue. `bin/start.mjs` supervises exactly two children
# — this process and the MCP face — and NOTHING ran either under systemd. So the two processes the door
# configures had no service to attach to, a hosted deployment kept them alive with a hand launcher, and
# `clearotron start`'s refusal had nothing to point at.
#
# ── ONE CONFIGURATION PER SERVER BOX (owner ruling, 2026-08-26) ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# `EnvironmentFile=%h/.env`, like prelim-driver.service, and the CF Access audience lives there. The
# alternative — explicit `Environment=` lines carrying the audience, as profile-service.service used to —
# existed to stop `~/.env` shadowing the trademark AUD. That protection was against a SECOND SOURCE OF
# TRUTH, and the ruling removes the second source rather than defending against it: a box with these
# units installed has one configuration and `clearotron start` now refuses on it outright.
[Unit]
Description=Clearotron portal — the UI, the API, the sign-in and the config surface
Documentation=https://github.com/CordilleraSarl/Clearotron/blob/main/docs/architecture/02-architecture.md
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target
# ── THE ENGINE DOOR FIRST, WHERE THERE IS ONE (tracker issue 222) ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# The units carried no ordering between them, so a simultaneous restart of the set started this process
# before the door it calls. Its boot probe then logged an outage — in the present tense, with "a
# clearance ordered from the portal returns 502" attached — on a box that was fine seconds later. It
# printed on every reboot and cost a diagnostic detour during the 0.1.6 production upgrade.
#
# `After=` AND NOT `Wants=`: this is ordering only. A portal serving with no engine door is a supported
# state — the pages work, only the Start button's upstream is missing — so pulling the door in as a
# dependency would change what installing this unit means. Naming a unit that is not installed is a
# no-op to systemd, which is what makes one line correct on every unit set: the packaged install has
# `clearotron-mcp-face.service`, and a deployment that runs the door under another name simply orders
# against nothing here.
#
# IT NARROWS THE RACE RATHER THAN CLOSING IT, and the other half of tracker issue 222 is why that is
# enough. `Type=simple` counts a unit as started once its process is forked, not once it is listening,
# so the door may still be binding when this starts. The probe's message no longer claims an outage for
# that, because the submit path re-probes per request and never consults the boot verdict.
After=clearotron-mcp-face.service

[Service]
Type=simple
EnvironmentFile=%h/.env
# BOTH DOCUMENTED INSTALL LAYOUTS, for the same reason prelim-driver.service carries this line: a reader
# who took the vendor's install script has the binary in ~/.local/bin, and one who took the npm route has
# it in ~/.npm-global/bin. INSTALL.md §1 names neither, so both are on the path.
Environment=PATH=%h/.local/bin:%h/.npm-global/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
# THIS deployment's configuration is the EnvironmentFile above and nothing else. portal-service.mjs is one
# of the CLI entries that reads <repo>/.env for a laptop first run (shared/env-local.mjs); a server must
# never take configuration from inside its own checkout, so a stray file left by a debugging session
# cannot quietly reconfigure the door.
Environment=CLEAROTRON_NO_ENV_FILE=1
# NO WorkingDirectory=, deliberately — systemd does not expand variables there, only in ExecStart
# arguments, and nothing here reads the working directory: the code finds itself from its own file URL.
ExecStart=/usr/bin/node ${CLEAROTRON_CHECKOUT_DIR}/driver/portal-service.mjs
# ── THIS UNIT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT WRITE THE CONFIGURATION CAPTURE ──────────────────────────────────
#
# It did, for about an hour, and that was a defect worth recording rather than quietly deleting.
#
# Under the design where the page RENDERED the capture, having the portal refresh it at start was the fix
# — it made the page current after a restart. The owner's 2026-09-05 ruling inverted that: the page now
# answers LIVE, and the capture's only remaining job is to be an INDEPENDENT WITNESS of what the engine
# last ran under, so the page can say when the two disagree.
#
# A witness the portal writes is not independent of the portal. The portal would capture its own
# environment at its own start and then, at request time, compare its own environment against it — two
# readings of one value, which agree by construction and always will. The row would render green on every
# box forever while measuring nothing, and the label the page gives it ("what the last run recorded")
# would be false as well.
#
# So the worker unit writes it and this one does not. `clearotron-worker.service` carries the
# ExecStartPost, and a run refreshes it after every drain — both of those are the engine, which is whose
# posture the row claims to report.
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=10

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
